<article class="env-lemma" id="0AN2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AN2">Lemma <span data-tag="0AN2">87.15.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of formal algebraic spaces over $S$. The diagonal morphism $\Delta : X \to X \times _ Y X$ is representable (by schemes), a monomorphism, locally quasi-finite, locally of finite type, and separated. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $T$ be a scheme and let $T \to X \times _ Y X$ be a morphism. Then 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  T \times _{(X \times _ Y X)} X = T \times _{(X \times _ S X)} X  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Hence the result follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AIP" data-tag="0AIP">87.11.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>